  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes with 5 tests, including 3 new regression tests.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a failed job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. Sync throws and plain return values also weren't handled. Each job now runs inside a promise. Its slot is freed whether it succeeds or fails, and only that job's own promise rejects.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending, not that nothing was running. It now waits for both.\n- **One job at a time after `resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled or the queue is empty or paused.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` check three things:\n- The queue keeps going after async and sync failures.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs.\n- `resume()` fills all four slots at concurrency 4.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.",
